  "body": "## Defect\n\n`pm-stack/opencode-claimant/claimant.py` read a session's messages from\n`GET {OPENCODE_URL}/api/session/<id>/messages` in two places:\n\n- `supervision_step()` — the #4758 \"verify zero messages first\" guard\n  (before deleting a bound session and atomically rebinding its task);\n- `_get_messages()` — the reconcile read `_send_prompt()` uses to decide\n  whether one resend is allowed.\n\nOn the standing laptop OpenCode v2 server that path does not exist: it\nreturns **HTTP 404 with a zero-byte body**. Both call sites ran curl\n*without* `-f` and then `json.loads(stdout or \"[]\")`, so the 404 parsed\nto `[]` — a confirmed \"zero messages\" that never happened. The correct\nendpoint is `GET /api/session/<id>/message`, which returns\n`{\"data\": [ ...messages... ], \"cursor\": {...}}`.\n\n## Live evidence (2026-11-09, http://127.0.0.1:13420)\n\nSampled four real sessions from `GET /api/session`:\n\n```\nses_e5e40adbccfffe5tL3Wrx51oUl  /messages 404 (0 bytes)  /message 200  n=100 at limit=100\nses_e5e403fe19cffeWYfpPV90r6Ta  /messages 404 (0 bytes)  /message 200  n=58\nses_e5e3fbfb4a1ffeHj2ReQt5sy1v  /messages 404 (0 bytes)  /message 200  n=17\nses_e5e403fe514ffeSDLSefGjZqEF  /messages 404 (0 bytes)  /message 200  n=89\n```\n\nThe default page is 20 messages; `?limit=100` returns the counts above,\nconfirming `/message` really carries the full list. (The task report\nencountered 29 and 25 messages for two other sessions; the point is the\nsame: `/messages` 404s, `/message` 200s with `{\"data\": [...]}`.)\n\n## Behavioural consequence\n\n1. The supervision guard was **inert**. A gone/idle bound session was\n   always judged \"zero messages\", so the loop could DELETE a session\n   that actually had messages and atomically clear its task binding\n   (`--launched-by opencode-claimant-recovery:zero-message-deleted`),\n   making the task relaunchable — the duplicate-execution defect the\n   ordering exists to prevent.\n2. `_get_messages()` returned `[]` instead of `None` when the read\n   failed, so `_send_prompt()` could POST a second prompt into a session\n   whose first prompt may already have landed.\n\nBoth docstrings already stated the intended rule: an unreadable session\nis **UNKNOWN**, never empty.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Both paths now use `GET /api/session/<id>/message`.\n- curl runs with `-f`, so any non-2xx is a failure.\n- Strict parsing: only a JSON object with a **list** under `data`\n  (unwrapped) or a bare JSON list is a confirmed read. Empty body,\n  non-JSON, dict without a list `data`, error object, or transport\n  failure returns `None` (UNKNOWN).\n- `supervision_step()` now calls `_get_messages()` (one shared\n  fail-closed parser) instead of its own curl/parse. `None` leaves the\n  task bound — printed as a note, no DELETE, no bind. Only a confirmed\n  `[]` enters the zero-message recovery path.\n- Added the missing lease guard: a bound task is recoverable only once\n  `poll.parse_lease_ms(task.get(\"lease_until\"))` is in the past.\n  An unparseable lease is **not** expired.\n- No functions renamed, no launch/bind logic changed.\n\n## Tests\n\n`pm-stack/opencode-claimant/test_claimant.py` harness updated to the\n`/message` endpoint and given `messages_rc` and a DELETE recorder.\nNew regression coverage:\n\n- 404 / empty-body read (return code non-zero, and also a 200 with an\n  empty body) → no candidate, no DELETE, no bind;\n- bound session that HAS messages → not recovered;\n- confirmed `{\"data\": []}`/`[]` → still recovers exactly as before\n  (DELETE then `bind ... --launched-by\n  opencode-claimant-recovery:zero-message-deleted`), including the\n  live 200 shape `{\"data\": [], \"cursor\": {}}`;\n- bound task with an unexpired lease → not recovered;\n- unparseable lease → not recovered.\n\nCommands run (Python 3.14.8 from the user environment; no pytest):\n\n```\npython3 -m py_compile pm-stack/opencode-claimant/claimant.py pm-stack/opencode-claimant/test_claimant.py\n  -> COMPILE_OK\n\npython3 -m unittest pm-stack/opencode-claimant/test_claimant.py\n  -> Ran 15 tests in 0.035s — OK (exit 0)\n\npython3 -m unittest pm-stack/opencode-claimant/test_poll.py\n  -> Ran 50 tests in 0.043s — OK (exit 0)\n```\n\n`ruff check` on the two files reports 49 findings, all pre-existing\ncategories (BLE001, PLW1510, UP006/UP035/UP045, DTZ003, EXE001, …); the\nrepo has no ruff config for this path and CI's format tier is not a\nmerge gate. No new finding category was introduced.\n\n## Not verified\n\n- I did not run the claimant in live mode against the real queue, so I\n  did not observe an actual recovery fire or delete on a production\n  session. The change was exercised only through the stubbed transport\n  test harness plus the direct live endpoint probes above.\n- I did not test a session with exactly zero messages on the live\n  server (none was convenient to create); the confirmed-empty shape is\n  covered by the unit tests.\n- Full repository test suite was not run — only the two claimant suites.\n\n## Open questions / defaults chosen\n\n- Note-only handling for an unknown supervision read (a `print`, not a\n  new skip record): supervision's return type is a candidate list and\n  `log_fire` is not threaded into it, so recording the skip would be a\n  larger change. Default: keep it a note, matching the file's existing\n  warning idiom.\n- Supervision reuses `_get_messages()` rather than duplicating the\n  parser. This is intentional so the two reads can never diverge again.\n- Lease expiry uses `time.time()` in milliseconds, matching\n  `poll.is_stuck_bound`'s `now_ms` convention.\n\nRefs #3026.\n",
